<title>UNITED NATIONS: US see no problem with Iraq oil-pricing formula.</title>
<headline>US see no problem with Iraq oil-pricing formula.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. official said he did not see any problem with the Iraq oil pricing formula, one element of implementing the delayed oil-for-food deal between Baghdad and the United Nations.</p>
<p>Edward Gnehm, the deputy permanent U.S. representative, told Reuters in answer to queries: &quot;I don't think there will be a problem. &quot;</p>
<p>He said that &quot;we have always said that when there was a realistic probability; that there would be implementation (of the deal) that we didn't have a problem in principle with the oil pricing formula.&quot;</p>
</text>
